---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { href, REPO, toolCount, VERSION } from "../lib/docs";

const site = (Astro.site?.href ?? "").replace(/\/$/, "") + import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "");
const win = `irm ${site}/install.ps1 | iex`;
const mac = `curl -fsSL ${site}/install.sh | bash`;
const tools = toolCount();
---
<Layout title="Photoshop MCP">
  <section class="hero">
    <h1>Design and retouch in Photoshop by describing it.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      An MCP server that lets Claude, ChatGPT and other AI assistants drive Adobe Photoshop. It turns briefs for posters,
      social graphics, composites and photo edits into layered documents, then inspects, exports and revises them.
    </p>
    <div class="cta">
      <a class="btn primary" href="#install">Install</a>
      <a class="btn" href={href("/docs/tools/")}>Browse {tools} tools</a>
      <a class="btn" href={REPO}>View on GitHub</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="install" aria-labelledby="install-h">
    <h2 id="install-h">Install</h2>
    <div class="install">
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Windows</h3>
        <p>Installs the server to <code>%LOCALAPPDATA%\PhotoshopMCP</code> and registers it with your AI clients.</p>
        <ol class="steps">
          <li>Press <kbd>Win</kbd>+<kbd>R</kbd>, type <strong>powershell</strong> and press <kbd>Enter</kbd> (no admin needed).</li>
          <li>Click <strong>Copy</strong> below, then paste into PowerShell with a right-click or <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>V</kbd>.</li>
          <li>Press <kbd>Enter</kbd> and wait for it to finish.</li>
        </ol>
        <div class="cmd"><code>{win}</code><button type="button" data-copy={win}>Copy</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>macOS</h3>
        <p>Installs the server to <code>~/Library/Application Support/PhotoshopMCP</code> and registers it with your AI clients.</p>
        <ol class="steps">
          <li>Press <kbd>Cmd</kbd>+<kbd>Space</kbd>, type <strong>Terminal</strong> and press <kbd>Enter</kbd>.</li>
          <li>Click <strong>Copy</strong> below, then paste into Terminal with <kbd>Cmd</kbd>+<kbd>V</kbd>.</li>
          <li>Press <kbd>Enter</kbd> and wait for it to finish.</li>
        </ol>
        <div class="cmd"><code>{mac}</code><button type="button" data-copy={mac}>Copy</button></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="note">
      Configures every MCP client it finds: Claude Desktop, Claude Code, Cursor, Windsurf, VS Code (Copilot), Cline, Roo Code,
      Gemini CLI and Codex. Existing configs are merged, with a backup. Scripts: <a href={href("/install.ps1")}>install.ps1</a>,
      <a href={href("/install.sh")}>install.sh</a>. <a href={href("/docs/configuration/#mcp-clients-the-installers-configure")}>Details</a>.
    </p>

    <div class="card stack">
      <h3>After install</h3>
      <ol class="steps">
        <li>Start <strong>Adobe Photoshop</strong> (tested with Photoshop 2027). Nothing needs installing inside Photoshop.</li>
        <li>On macOS, allow Terminal or Node to control Photoshop when asked (System Settings → Privacy &amp; Security → Automation).</li>
        <li>Fully quit and reopen your MCP client, then ask: <em>"Check the Photoshop status, then make a 1080×1080 poster that says 'Summer Sale'."</em></li>
      </ol>
    </div>

    <div class="card stack">
      <h3>Manual install</h3>
      <p>Needs Git, Node.js 20+ and pnpm (via Corepack).</p>
      <ol class="steps">
        <li>Clone the repo: <code>git clone {REPO}.git</code>, then <code>cd Photoshop-MCP</code>.</li>
        <li>Install and build: <code>corepack enable</code>, <code>pnpm install</code>, <code>pnpm build</code>.</li>
        <li>Register it with Claude Desktop: <code>scripts\install.ps1 -ConfigureClaude</code> on Windows or <code>./scripts/install.sh --configure-claude</code> on macOS.</li>
        <li>Check the setup: <code>scripts\diagnostics.ps1</code> or <code>./scripts/diagnostics.sh</code>.</li>
        <li>Then follow the <strong>After install</strong> steps above.</li>
      </ol>
      <p class="note">Full guide, ChatGPT and remote HTTP: <a href={href("/docs/installation/")}>installation guide</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="what-h">
    <h2 id="what-h">What it does</h2>
    <div class="features">
      <div class="card"><div class="stat">{tools}</div><p>MCP tools: documents, layers, text, shapes, selections and masks, retouching, color correction, filters, compositing, smart objects, actions, batch processing and exports.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><div class="stat">Plans</div><p>A design engine turns a brief into a structured plan (layout, type scale, palette) you can review before anything is drawn.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><div class="stat">Editable</div><p>Everything is native Photoshop layers, adjustment layers and smart objects, named, not a flattened image, so you can keep working by hand.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><div class="stat">Checked</div><p>Results come from Photoshop itself. Previews, critiques and automatic fixes close the loop, and file access is limited to folders you allow.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="how-h">
    <h2 id="how-h">How it works</h2>
    <ol class="flow">
      <li>You ask your assistant for a design.</li>
      <li>The server plans it and validates the plan.</li>
      <li>Photoshop builds it through COM (Windows) or AppleScript (macOS).</li>
      <li>The assistant inspects a preview and revises.</li>
    </ol>
    <p class="note">Details: <a href={href("/docs/architecture/")}>architecture</a>, <a href={href("/docs/examples/")}>example prompts</a>, <a href={href("/docs/limitations/")}>limitations</a>. Current release: <a href={`${REPO}/releases/latest`}>v{VERSION}</a>.</p>
  </section>

  <script>
    for (const btn of document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>("button[data-copy]")) {
      btn.addEventListener("click", async () => {
        try {
          await navigator.clipboard.writeText(btn.dataset.copy ?? "");
          btn.textContent = "Copied";
        } catch {
          btn.textContent = "Select it";
        }
        setTimeout(() => (btn.textContent = "Copy"), 1600);
      });
    }
  </script>
</Layout>
